Source dataset
--------------

  Online Retail
  Chen, D. (2015). UCI Machine Learning Repository.
  DOI: 10.24432/C5BW33   https://doi.org/10.24432/C5BW33
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)

The dataset is not redistributed in this repository. scripts/get_data.py
downloads it at build time into data/raw/, which .gitignore keeps out of
git.

What this project does with it, so the attribution is accurate about what
was changed: rows are filtered against nine quality rules (cancellations,
non-positive quantity or price, duplicates, price outliers, non-product
stock codes), the survivors are reshaped into a star schema with a derived
continuous calendar and surrogate keys, and the invoice lines are
aggregated into baskets for the market-basket model. The published tables
and every figure in reports/ are therefore derived from the dataset, not
copies of it.

This file exists because the note used to sit at the bottom of LICENSE,
which stopped GitHub's licence detector recognising the text as MIT - the
repository was labelled "Other". A licence file should be the licence.
